<title>CHILE: Copper prices seen averaging about $1.00 per lb.</title>
<headline>Copper prices seen averaging about $1.00 per lb.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>World copper prices next year will average between $1.00 and $1.05 per pound, said the private trade group National Mining Society, or SONAMI.</p>
<p>The price prediction was contained in a SONAMI study and was announced at a news conference by its president Hernan Hochschild. The group has an important research department.</p>
<p>''We see supply and demand growing at similar levels next year,'' said Hochschild.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
